  "method": "Researched via live web search against each brand's own product pages (brand site first; a major retailer only where the brand has none, e.g. Threshold/Target, Mainstays/Walmart, Rivet/Amazon). For each candidate product the search tool returned text quoted from the live page (price, overall W/D/H, seat/cushion count, MSRP). Every figure recorded here was read from that page text, not estimated; inches were converted to cm at x2.54 and rounded to 1 decimal. Where a brand shows a 'member'/'sale' price next to a crossed-out 'regular'/'original' figure, the regular/original figure was recorded as price (not the temporary discount), except for a few perpetual direct-to-consumer storefronts (Structube, La-Z-Boy, Joybird, Walker Edison, Bush Furniture, South Shore, Hooker MSRP where shown) where the 'original'/'regular' figure shown alongside a lower current figure was likewise used as the recorded price. Per the task rules, seats is set to 1 for every armchair/diningChair/officeChair (fixed by definition) and is left null for sofas and dining tables unless the page explicitly stated a seat or cushion count (e.g. Burrow Nomad is explicitly marketed 'three-seater', Room & Board Metro is explicitly the 'two-cushion' Metro sofa, Structube SOFT and FALCON are explicitly '3-seater'). flatPack is true only where a page explicitly used assembly/unassembled language (Bush Furniture's bookcases: 'delivered unassembled'/'requires assembly'; Branch's two office chairs: ship with tools included and require assembly; Walker Edison's dining table, bookshelf and two dressers: brand-wide 'Easy Assembly'/'assembly required' language on its own product and policy pages) and left null everywhere else, where nothing equivalent was read. taxIncluded is false throughout (no page stated a tax-inclusive price). Brands tried and dropped for lack of a trustworthy price+dimension pair on their own page: Pottery Barn (Bander/Benchwright/Toscana tables returned internally inconsistent width/depth figures across snippets), Thomasville (site states prices vary by retailer and aren't published online), Mobilia and Interior Define (site-restricted search returned no indexable product pages, only third-party resale listings), Lovesac (Sactional pricing/seat-count is per module; no single overall W/D/H was found for a seat+side configuration), Amazon Rivet (Amazon prices fluctuate hourly; no stable 'regular' price could be confirmed, only a third-party price-history estimate), Flexispot (dimension snippets returned were inconsistent/implausible for the chairs priced), Target/Threshold Copley chair (price found but no overall width was ever returned, only seat width), The Brick (sofas and dining tables returned with name-only width, e.g. '78 inch', but no matching depth/height), Zinus office chairs (none found; used their one accent chair instead). CB2's 'set of 4' and Target's '2-pack' style listings are recorded as a single priced unit (the whole set) with that noted in variant/name, matching how the brand itself prices the SKU.",
